# =============================================================================
# GoldenCheetah Configuration Template
# =============================================================================
#
# PURPOSE:
#   GoldenCheetah is a powerful sports bike computer application. It does NOT
#   have a traditional configuration file. As stated in the official documentation
#   and manpage (GoldenCheetah(1)): "There are no options."
#
#   This template exists solely as a placeholder or for environment variable
#   injection if the Ansible role wraps the application. It is intentionally
#   empty of runtime directives because the application reads settings from
#   the GUI, internal database, or command-line arguments only.
#
# USAGE:
#   If this role needs to pass environment variables to the GoldenCheetah
#   process, add them below using the standard export syntax.
#   Example:
#     export GC_DATA_DIR="{{ gc_data_dir | default('/home/user/GC') }}"

# =============================================================================
# Environment Variables (Optional)
# =============================================================================
# Note: GoldenCheetah does not officially support a config file.
# These are provided as convenience if the orchestrator requires env vars.

# Path to the GoldenCheetah data directory (where training files are stored)
# Default: /home/user/GC
{% set gc_data_dir = gc_data_dir | default('/home/user/GC') %}
# GC_DATA_DIR="{{ gc_data_dir }}"

# =============================================================================
# End of Template
# =============================================================================